Rast wrote on 09/15/2003 06:20 PM:
[wishing spoiler]
> (At the risk of restarting a Holy War) +3 enchantment and 3 items give the 
> highest expected values, so the list should use those instead of +2/2.

I don't understand how the average can affect your individual game--you
don't get the average, you get what you get. If I always wish for 4
items I may get the best average, i.e. the biggest number of items, but
I would prefer more evenly distributed values, so that everything that I
wish for has a good chance of being more than one. Chances are I won't
have much more use of having four of something (worth wishing for, with
1 exception--?oC) but will likely be glad to have 2 of most things. This
means not that I will sneeze at 4 !oGA--but I prefer the situation of
havin 2 of them and 2 of something else or other.

Similarly for enchantment, +2 or +3 (which has the best average) is not
as important as the bigger jump from +0. If one was to wish up all
his/her armor kit, one would go for +3 to get the better average. For
other uses I would stick with +2.

Anyway thats IMO (and I am already sorry for writing it:) and as pointed
out elsewhere, I have changed the wording to "Opinions differ on...". If
you want 4/+3 (or any other combination) there's nothing easier than
s/^2/4 and s/+2/3. If there's extreme need it's possible to alternate
the number between versions or list items to be politically correct:-)

